This looks like April 2020. Equities rebounded 12.7% in the latest month after a -10.8% three-month return, and the VIX is 31. The fed funds rate is 0.04% and the 10-year yield is 0.63%, both consistent with April 2020. The unemployment rate of 4.4% looks like March 2020 data, and the payroll average of -70k fits a 3-month average that includes the March drop. The industrial production YoY of -5.49% is consistent with March or April 2020.

Headline CPI of 1.52% is the March 2020 figure. The April 2020 CPI was 0.33%, and it had not been published by the end of April. The snapshot is therefore consistent with April 2020, using the latest published values. The equity 1m return of +12.7% matches April 2020, when the S&P rose about 12.8%.


